What changed, in short:

- Waze's next turn and distance on BMW's own HUD arrows: a native HUD
  backend (hudguide, ProjectedModeGuiding, the default) and an optional
  drawn-image backend, with the readers for the CarPlay card and the Waze
  cluster map.
- Its own ids and on-unit names, so it installs beside the original:
  waze-on-cluster -> jap-waze-on-cluster (tool, units, drop-ins, paths under
  /var/opt, /run and /dev/shm, the local.conf, backups *.jap-orig),
  robertn_waze_cluster -> jap_waze_cluster (app, new RHMI UUIDs, title
  "Waze HUD").
- A guard against the original Waze on cluster (patch/conflict.js): dormant
  while it is installed, a pop-up in the app to remove it or cancel.
- cluster-render is kept unmodified, to build against only; it is not
  published from here.

